We disagree here; too high XLs I'd consider only to be if one happens
to have quite some random (i.e. not coupled with monster kills) gain
level enhancements (potions, etc.). Monster generation is very well
balanced (ignoring polytraps and shape-changers).

> soldier ants and mumaks are no joke at DL7.

They are no joke even at DL12, but that's independent of the racket;
soldier ants are a) very fast, b) come in swarms, c) are poisonous.
Mumaks hit extreemly hard but can regularily be avoided if one flees
or is performing a ranged attack instead of trying to melee.

> Even with high HPs, each can take a moderately ACed and burdened
> character (or pet) down before you can get rid of them.

(See above.)

> I simply posit that in mid game an unburdened, AC -10, XL7 character
> with an XL9 pet and full spellcasting ability is better equipped to deal
> than a AC 1 (or zero), burdened XL10 one with an XL5 pet and impacted
> with spellcasting. The former can run faster, take more hits, and still
> have lower level monsters than the latter.

Frankly, that argument is quite constructed. First, burdened is a
status that is nowhere inherent to non-PR players; that should be
generally avoided. Then, spellcasting is not the only ranged means
against monsters; and even if you rely on that (you said you were
biased because of the classes you play) just engrave the E-word and
zap away. The AC assumption seems inaccurate, given that you want
to avoid spellcasting problems. Anyway, I wouldn't want to meet a
swarm of soldier ants if I am not sufficiently fast and have some
effective means (highly enchanted artifacts, offensive wands from
Sokoban, etc.) to kill them, or a reliable way to engrave, or a way
to recover; an AC difference of 5..9 points had (in my experience)
never been the key part to survive soldier ants.

